Solve the system of equations:
\[
\left\{
\begin{matrix}
x^2(y+3) = 4(2-y) \\
y^2(z+3) = 4(2-z) \\
z^2(x+3) = 4(2-x)
\end{matrix}
\right.
\]

Evaluate the alternating sum:
\[ \sum_{k=0}^n (-1)^k \binom{m}{n-k} \binom{m}{k} = \begin{cases} 
(-1)^{\frac{n}{2}} \binom{m}{n/2} & \text{if } n \text{ is even} \\
0 & \text{if } n \text{ is odd}
\end{cases} \]

Given \(a, b, c, x, y, z \in \mathbb{R}\) and the conditions:
\[
\begin{cases}
ax + by + cz = 0 \\
a + b + c = \frac{1}{2017}
\end{cases}
\]
Find the value of \(Q = \frac{ax^2 + by^2 + cz^2}{ab(x - y)^2 + bc(y - z)^2 + ca(z - x)^2}\).
